🔐 Custom Domain Setup
Using Netlify:
bash
1. Buy domain from Namecheap/GoDaddy/Cloudflare ($8-15/year)
2. In Netlify: Site settings → Domain management
3. Add custom domain
4. Update DNS records:
   - Type: A → Points to Netlify IP
   - Type: CNAME → your-site.netlify.app
5. Wait 5-30 minutes for propagation
Using GitHub Pages:
bash
1. Go to repository Settings → Pages
2. Under Custom domain, enter your-domain.com
3. Add CNAME file to repository
4. Configure DNS:
   - Type: A → 185.199.108.153, 185.199.109.153, etc.
   - OR Type: CNAME → username.github.io
